    "docs/OBJECTS.md": [
      {
        "line": 13,
        "text": "| SETTLE-BOUND-20261126-001/1 | A bound on the round at which a local reader's view of a growth settles, from the start's largest block (live start knots sharing a neighbour, or a round-1 birth's fresh count) | All 3,157 five-knot census starts and a seeded sample of 1,000 of the 82,656 six-knot starts, under not-all-equal and parity, to round 24 | settling: from round K each kind's count is the fitted polynomial of degree at most D - 1 through the last round read | Refuted: settling past M + 5 (M + 7 with parents) in 41 of 1,556 five-knot and 6 of 387 six-knot starts of a dimension (11 and 2 under parity), by up to three rounds; most late starts narrow to a single birth a round first; the pair rule holds wherever views settle by the cut | refuted | [research/SETTLE-BOUND-20261126-001/README.md](../research/SETTLE-BOUND-20261126-001/README.md) |"
      }
    ],
    "docs/RESEARCH_GOALS.md": [
      {
        "line": 6155,
        "text": "| 2026-11-26 | [When a local reader's view settles, from the start alone](../research/SETTLE-BOUND-20261126-001/decision.md) | G17, G1 | Obstruction learned | A check by the thread at the coordinator's go-ahead (computed; referee pending). A bound frozen on starts of up to four knots, a view settling within the start's largest block plus 5 rounds (plus 7 with parents), fails on 41 of 1,556 five-knot and 6 of 387 held-out six-knot starts of a dimension under not-all-equal (11 and 2 under parity). Most late starts narrow to a single birth a round before going on as a lone knot, late even with no large block. The look-alike pair rule holds wherever views settle by the cut. Successor: the round of the last merge as the bound. |"
      }
    ],
